Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:25:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple-vxd: Add the HEVC command-stream builder

AppleD5500 decodes HEVC with a register program of its own, distinct
from the AVC one: per slice segment a chunk with the 0x90000000
descriptor, the whole slice NAL by DMA ({0xb0000001, header bits, bytes}
and {0xa.., address}), the 0x30xx/0x34xx command registers and a slice
structure the core copies into the picture's slice parameter buffer
(0xf), each with a kind-1 packet (mailbox 0x81); then one chunk of
single register writes for the picture, the 0x50xx/0x54xx entropy and
0x70xx/0x71xx render registers with the output and reference surfaces
and the scaling lists, with a kind-4 packet (mailbox 0x88) that ends the
job.  The layouts come from the iOS 16.7.10 kext (picture path
0xfffffff0062960a0, per slice 0x62b37d4, per picture 0x62b7ab0) and are
listed register by register in the comments.

This builds that program from the V4L2 HEVC controls.  It is pure code,
like the H.264 builder, so it also builds on the host: a harness feeds
it x265 and VideoToolbox test streams and compares every command word,
slice structure and packet against an independent generator written from
the kext.

Supported: 8-bit 4:2:0, I/P/B, multiple and dependent slice segments,
tiles, WPP, long-term references, weighted prediction, PCM and scaling
lists.  Refused: other chroma formats and bit depths (the Main 10 output
layout is not established), more than 15 references.

The 15 hardware reference slots are named by the V4L2 DPB index; the
kext numbers them in its own DPB order, which never leaves the host.

Nothing calls the builder yet.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #121, commit 4016f5e2; unchanged]

